body:
On v0.10.0, `immutable_store.local.max_size` is documented as "Maximum total store size in bytes before background compaction reclaims space", but the compactor compares it against `packstore_total_size()`, which only sums `group.packstore.total_size()`. Loose fragments and the index aren't counted.

On a store of 2.3 MB across 285 files:
```
Packstore compactor skipping, current size 1661 is below threshold 1048576
```
With `max_size = 1 MiB`, the pass never ran even though the store was more than twice the cap. A store can exceed max_size on disk while the packstore stays under it, so compaction never fires and the cap has no effect.

lore-storage/src/local/immutable_store.rs:
```rust
pub async fn packstore_total_size(&self) -> usize {
    let mut total_size = 0;
    for group in self.group.iter() {
        total_size += group.packstore.total_size().await.unwrap_or_default();
    }
    total_size
}
```
`compact_packfiles` compares `total_size < max_size` to decide whether to run.

Proposed: either the trigger accounts for the whole store, or the docs state the cap applies only to the packstore.
